+# ExcelBuildMode 1.3.5 — Windows-safe directory sync (design note)
+
+An Excel plugin note for Wink Reyes Valley. November 14, 2026.
+Lane 2 of the P-FSYNC-1 sweep, from the mirror storage-cause diagnosis
+in `~/workspace/mirror-storage-diagnosis-20261114/DIAGNOSIS.md`.
+
+## The failure this fixes
+
+The durable stores end every save by fsync-ing the containing directory
+(`FileChannel.open(directory, READ)` + `force(true)`) so the directory
+entry itself is durable. That is legal on Linux, where the live server
+runs, and impossible via Java NIO on Windows: the directory open itself
+throws `AccessDeniedException`. On the PC test-server mirror the Nov 13
+boot shows the result verbatim — `RecoveryJournal.forceDirectory` →
+`FileChannel.open` → `AccessDeniedException:
+plugins\ExcelBuildMode\recovery` — and the plugin degrades: storage is
+reported unavailable and new Build entry is disabled. A minimal Java
+probe on the PC (diagnosis) reproduced it exactly, and confirmed the
+other half of the picture: create + write + fsync + delete of a FILE in
+the same directory works fine. Only directory channels are refused.
+
+Two boot ERRORs in the same log have a different, simpler cause and are
+NOT this fix's subject: `ReviewHoldStore` / `BuildReturnStore`
+constructor refusals ("directory is unavailable") fire because those
+two directories were never provisioned on the mirror (the mirror tree
+carries `recovery\` and `active-index\` only). The constructors'
+provision-first refusal is deliberate design ("missing storage is not
+an empty history") and is unchanged; the mirror rig provisions the two
+directories, as the live installation did. What this fix removes is
+those stores' save path failing on Windows once provisioned.
+
+## The change (the whole delta vs 1.3.4)
+
+One new package-private helper, `core/DirectorySync.bestEffort(Path)`:
+attempt the directory open + force exactly as before, tolerate any
+`IOException` from it. Four call-site conversions, no signature changes:
+
+- `RecoveryJournal.forceDirectory` — delegates. Covers the constructor
+  probe and every journal save (begin ×3, writeState).
+- `ActiveSessionIndex.force` — delegates. A fourth durable store the
+  diagnosis never reached: it is constructed immediately after the
+  journal in the same enable block, so the journal failure masked it;
+  its constructor and every save force the root directory the same way.
+- `ReviewHoldStore.hold` — the inline post-move directory force now
+  delegates.
+- `BuildReturnStore.record` — the inline post-move directory force now
+  delegates.
+
+Unchanged, deliberately: every file-level `channel.force(true)` stays
+mandatory and in place; the atomic-move writes are untouched; on Linux
+the directory force still runs (nothing about live behavior changes).
+Version 1.3.4 → 1.3.5 in plugin.yml (plus an appended description
+sentence), the two startup banner strings, and the two test version
+pins. New suite `DirectorySyncTests` (see below); the eight carried
+suites are otherwise unmodified and hold their 1.3.4 totals.
+
+## Swept and deliberately excluded
+
+A full-tree sweep found one more directory force:
+`PlayerDataProof.forceVerifiedMarker` fsyncs the playerdata file and
+then its parent directory (line 75). It is NOT converted. That method
+is not a store save — it is a fail-closed verification proof whose
+contract is "fsync that same inode and parent directory, and reject
+detectable replacement/change"; the post-force byte and stamp
+re-checks are the safety property. Weakening its directory force to
+best-effort would silently loosen a proof other flows rely on. On
+Windows it keeps failing closed during recovery verification; changing
+that is a separate design call for the supervisor, not a rider on this
+fix.
+
+## Proof shape
+
+- Base gate: the unmodified 1.3.4 tree (copied from
+  `~/workspace/buildmode-134-build/`) rebuilt byte-identical to the
+  on-record candidate (SHA-256 39d86f3b…) before any edit.
+- Nine suites via build.sh: the eight carried suites at their 1.3.4
+  totals (CoreTests 5,710; RewardTests 5,283; RecoverySafetyTests 84;
+  PlayerDataProofTests 145; PilotGateTests 338; BuildReturnTests 18;
+  AdminTests 82, version pin moved; ReviewedTests 25) + NEW
+  DirectorySyncTests 14: the unguarded idiom provably throws where a
+  directory cannot be opened; bestEffort tolerates that failure
+  (repeatedly, and without creating anything); save round-trips through
+  all four stores (hold, build-return record, journal begin/complete,
+  index begin/complete).
+- Deterministic: in-place double-build and a clean-room rebuild both
+  reproduce the candidate hash (BUILD-RECORD.md in the fix folder).
+- Rig verification still owed (supervisor's step): a mirror boot with
+  1.3.5 and the two unprovisioned directories provisioned must show
+  zero storage ERRORs and enabled Build entry — the Windows half of
+  the proof can only run on the PC.
